 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "How did a six-hundred-year empire end?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Quietly, on a British warship. In November 1922, the last sultan left Istanbul."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "What happened to the empire?",
   "scene": "start",
   "date": "1918",
   "place": "Ottoman lands"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "It lost the First World War. In 1918 it signed an armistice, and Allied troops took over Istanbul."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "The sultan was Mehmed the Sixth. In 1920 his government signed the Treaty of Sèvres.",
   "scene": "sebah",
   "date": "1920",
   "place": "Istanbul",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.35,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.28,
     1.3
    ]
   },
   "say": "The sultan was Mehmed the Sixth. In 1920 his government signed the Treaty of Sevres."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "What did that treaty do?",
   "scene": "sevres",
   "date": "1920",
   "place": "Anatolia"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "It carved up even Anatolia, among Greece, Italy, France and a new Armenia. The straits went under foreign control."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Did people accept that?",
   "scene": "war",
   "date": "1920–1922",
   "place": "Ankara"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "No. In Ankara, a new parliament led by Mustafa Kemal rejected it and fought a war of independence. By September 1922, it had won."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And the sultan?",
   "scene": "mehmed6",
   "date": "1 November 1922",
   "place": "Ankara",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.33,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "In November 1922, the assembly in Ankara abolished the sultanate."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Two weeks later, Mehmed the Sixth left on the British battleship Malaya, bound for Malta. He died in exile in Italy in 1926.",
   "scene": "malta",
   "date": "November 1922",
   "place": "Malta",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So what replaced the empire?",
   "scene": "end",
   "date": "1923",
   "place": "Turkey"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "In 1923, the Treaty of Lausanne set the borders of a new state, and on the twenty-ninth of October, the Republic of Turkey was proclaimed."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "From Osman to Mehmed the Sixth: six hundred and twenty-three years.",
   "scene": "years",
   "date": ""
  },
  {
